<title>USA: Emcor names Levy as president.</title>
<headline>Emcor names Levy as president.</headline>
<dateline>NORWALK, Conn. 1997-04-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Emcor Group Inc said it elevated Jeffrey Levy, its executive vice president, to president, succeeding Frank MacInnis.</p>
<p>MacInnis remains chairman and chief executive officer.</p>
<p>Levy will retain the position of chief operating officer, a job he has held since 1994.</p>
<p>Before joining Emcor in 1992, Levy was executive vice president and chief operating officer of Lehrer McGovern Bovis, the construction management company.</p>
<p>Emcor is engaged in mechanical and electrical construction and facilities services.</p>
</text>
